  "content": {
    "id": "p55-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The polynomial $P(x)$ is given by $P(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx-18$.\nFind $a$ and $b$ given that $(x+2)$ is a factor of $P(x)$,\nand $-24$ is the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $x-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2,\\ b=-9$. Use $P(-2)=0$ and $P(1)=-24$.",
      "worked": "By the factor theorem, $P(-2)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=(-2)^3+a(-2)^2+b(-2)-18,\\\\0&=-8+4a-2b-18,\\\\4a-2b&=26.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the remainder theorem, $P(1)=-24$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1+a+b-18,\\\\-24&=a+b-17,\\\\a+b&=-7.\\end{align*}$$\nAdding twice the second equation to the first:\n$$\\begin{align*}6a&=12,\\\\a&=2,\\\\b&=-7-2=-9.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
